{"mathdb_id": 356099, "uuid": "781667d4-edce-4326-91fd-bc96a81b34e0", "canonical_url": "https://mathdb.com/p/356099/linear-hadwiger-s-conjecture", "title": "Linear Hadwiger's conjecture", "statement": "Let $K_t$ be the complete graph on $t$ vertices, and call a graph $K_t$-minor-free if it has no $K_t$ minor. A graph is $k$-colourable if it has a proper colouring using at most $k$ colours. **Linear Hadwiger's conjecture.** There exists a constant $C>0$ such that for every integer $t\geqslant1$, every $K_t$-minor-free graph is $Ct$-colourable. This is a natural weakening of Hadwiger's conjecture. The best known general upper bounds are superlinear, so the conjecture remains open.", "statement_completeness": "full", "post_type": "conjecture", "status": "open", "tags": ["graph-colouring", "graph-minors"], "importance": "corpus", "source_name": "Yangyan Gu, Yiting Jiang, David R. Wood and Xuding Zhu, “Refined list version of Hadwiger's conjecture”, arXiv:2209.07013 (2022).", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.07013", "first_stated_year": 2011, "first_stated_year_source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.07013", "documented_by_year": null, "documented_by_source_url": null, "references": "**7 papers in this index state this conjecture** (2011–2022). The statement above is taken from the most recent of them; the others are [arXiv:2110.09403](https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.09403), [arXiv:2108.01633](https://arxiv.org/abs/2108.01633), [arXiv:2010.05999](https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.05999), [arXiv:2004.10367](https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.10367), [arXiv:1910.09378](https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.09378), [arXiv:1110.2272](https://arxiv.org/abs/1110.2272).

